# Semgrep already excludes some paths by default (e.g. /tests, /test, /vendors).
# This only affects `semgrep scan` target discovery -- confirmed in docs/FINDINGS.md
# that `semgrep --test` / `semgrep --validate` still see rules/ directly since they
# take it as an explicit --config path, not a scanned target.

# Reference/fixed-state files are not scan targets -- they exist only to show
# "what the clean version looks like" and would otherwise double-count as zero-finding
# noise in every pack run.
*.example

# Documentation and vendored (offline) rule snapshots are not scan targets.
docs/
vendor/semgrep-rules/

# Custom rule test fixtures intentionally contain bad patterns (fake secrets, bad
# configs) to exercise ruleid/ok assertions -- excluded from whole-repo pack scans
# (e.g. p/secrets, p/security-audit) so they don't show up as unrelated noise.
rules/
